                                             <ul class="notification-message no-margin"><li>If current conditions in the Middle East impact your ability to attend your scheduled test, please contact ETS for support and rescheduling options. Your safety is our priority.
</li><li>Taking the GRE庐 General Test at home is a safe and convenient option for students who prefer to take their test at home rather than at a test center. The test is available worldwide in all locations where the GRE General Test is normally available. Start your registration here in your ETS account and select the At Home option on the Find Test Centers and Dates page.</li>
<li>Students taking a GRE at home test should review and confirm that their equipment meets all technical requirements and review instructions for the new second-camera feature (effective January 5, 2026), as well as all environmental guidelines by visiting <a href="Taking" the="" gre="" general="" test="" at="" home="">Equipment and environment requirements for at home testing.</a></li></ul>

                                             
